      "path": "email-and-test-inbox/SKILL.md",
      "sha256": "440d7f08e21be5d23d9218944b1e80bd4050134b6a8dba36bc789646a5ad1908",
      "content": "---\nname: email-and-test-inbox\ndescription: When the app sends email, or you need to test sign-up, magic-link, or reset mail without a real mailbox.\n---\n\n# Send email and read the test inbox\n\n## Send\n\n```ts\n// api/_lib/order-email.ts — call it from a handler that already checked who\n// receives this; the address comes from your saved order, never the request.\nexport function sendOrderShipped(\n  sw: SomewhereRuntimeContext,\n  order: { id: string; email: string; trackingNumber: string },\n): Promise<SomewhereEmailSendResult> {\n  return sw.email.send({\n    to: order.email,\n    subject: 'Your order shipped',\n    text: `Tracking: ${order.trackingNumber}`, // or html, or both\n    reply_to: 'support@yourapp.com', // optional\n    idempotency_key: `order-shipped:${order.id}`,\n  });\n}\n```\n\nIt can only email people registered with this project (including pending magic-link sign-ins) or the project's owner.\n\n## Test inbox\n\nAddresses `<anything>@<project-subdomain>.test.somewhere.site` never reach a real mailbox. Read it with `somewhere email test-inbox <address>` (or `sw.email.inbox(address)`) → `{ address, messages: [{ id, to, subject, text, html, magic_link, created_at }] }`.\n\n## Failure 1: MANAGED_SENDER_RECIPIENT_NOT_A_USER\n\nOther recipients return `MANAGED_SENDER_RECIPIENT_NOT_A_USER`; verify your own sender domain for outreach.\n\n## Failure 2: gating on status 'sent'\n\nDo not gate follow-up work on `status === 'sent'` alone: a captured test send and a replay of a delivered message are both successful sends.\n\nSources (`somewhere docs <topic>`): sw.email.\n"
